  "explanation": "Choice C is correct. The $y$-intercept of the graph of $h$ occurs where $x = 0$. To find this, we evaluate $h(0)$. Since $h(x) = f(x + 2)$, we have $h(0) = f(0 + 2) = f(2)$. The transformation $h(x) = f(x + 2)$ shifts the graph of $f$ horizontally $2$ units to the left. From the equation $f(x) = -(x - 1)(x - 3)$, we can calculate: $f(2) = -(2 - 1)(2 - 3) = -(1)(-1) = 1$. Therefore, the $y$-coordinate of the point at which the graph of $h$ intersects the $y$-axis is $1$.",
